smsc911x: pulse the LAN9221 reset line the way the vendor 4.14 kernel does.
The RW20 DT flags the reset gpio active-high while the LAN9221 reset pin is
active-low, so devm_gpiod_get_optional(..., GPIOD_OUT_LOW) leaves the chip held
in reset. Drive 0, wait 100 ms, then 1 so the line ends high (chip out of reset).
Source: comment in the patch; status doc lists it as applying cleanly to 7.3.4.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/smsc/smsc911x.c	2026-11-15 11:37:04.856900019 -0500
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/smsc/smsc911x.c	2026-11-15 11:37:04.860900326 -0500
@@ -439,6 +439,15 @@
 	pdata->reset_gpiod = devm_gpiod_get_optional(&pdev->dev,
 						     "reset",
 						     GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
+	/* The RW20 DT flags this line active-high while the LAN9221 reset
+	 * pin is active-low: requesting it OUT_LOW holds the chip in reset.
+	 * Reproduce the vendor kernel's pulse, which ends with the line high.
+	 */
+	if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(pdata->reset_gpiod)) {
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(pdata->reset_gpiod, 0);
+		msleep(100);
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(pdata->reset_gpiod, 1);
+	}
 
 	/* Request clock */
 	pdata->clk = clk_get(&pdev->dev, NULL);
